<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner wins China dam project contract.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins China dam project contract.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian industrial group Kvaerner ASA said on Monday its technology had been selected for eight of the 14 first turbines to be delivered to China's giant Three Gorges dam project.</p>
<p>&quot;The core components for five turbines will be produced under the leadership of Kvaerner Energy in Norway and China,&quot; the company said in a statement to the Oslo Bourse.</p>
<p>&quot;The other three turbines will be produced by GEC Alsthom based on Kvaerner design. The total value of the contract is 300 million crowns,&quot; Kvaerner said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
